        "beats": [
          {
            "id": "S03_02",
            "vo": "The simplest thing the app can do is save it as it is. One column for your email, one for your password."
          },
          {
            "id": "S03_03",
            "vo": "It works. You log in. The app compares what you typed with what it saved, and lets you in."
          },
          {
            "id": "S03_04",
            "vo": "It also means anyone who copies that table walks away with every password in it. That was Rock You."
          },
          {
            "id": "S03_05",
            "vo": "And attackers try leaked passwords on other sites. If you reused yours, one leak can open those accounts too."
          }
        ]
